  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(4,35).$ So, our actual value is $y=35.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=4$ has the $y$-coordinate $40.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=40.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250390/assets/03fc54d7e01a74be510f951abbe7c305e605e45ccd8db49e69610b3434d97835.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =35-40 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $\\$(-5\\,000).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
